\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Projected total gas column density for an infinitesimally thin, $1\,M_\odot $ shell. The colour scale is logarithmic and spans the 2nd to 99.5th percentiles of non-zero map values: $-2.130 \leq \log _{10}(\Sigma _{\rm  LOS}/\mathrm  {g\,cm^{-2}}) \leq -1.005$. White is outside the projected surface. Bright rims arise from the $1/|\hat  n\cdot \hat  \ell |$ projection factor.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
