\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Finite-duration ($\Delta T=20$ yr) ejection model. The logarithmic scale spans the 2nd to 99.5th percentiles of non-zero pixels. Relative to the infinitesimal shell, the limb contribution is spread over the radial width of the flow rather than concentrated in a single surface.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Observer-facing component of the $\Delta T=20$ yr model with a $10^\circ $ equatorial cutoff applied only to this near-side selection. The all-crossing maps retain the complete supplied angular distribution. The scale is logarithmic and spans the 2nd to 99.5th percentiles of non-zero pixels: $-2.708 \leq \log _{10}(\Sigma _{\rm  LOS}/\mathrm  {g\,cm^{-2}}) \leq -1.592$.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
